cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use zwingen in academic work, please cite both the software and the accompanying methodological note."
title: "zwingen: Compositional, reproducible numerical primitives for empirical research"
abstract: >-
  zwingen provides a compositional layer of differentiable numerical
  primitives with bitwise reproducibility receipts. It targets empirical
  economists, statisticians, and scientific software engineers who need
  verifiable numerical contracts on top of JAX, optax, and numpyro.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/olaflaitinen/zwingen"
url: "https://zwingen.dev"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-05-03"
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - numerical-methods
  - econometrics
  - jax
  - optax
  - numpyro
  - bayesian-inference
  - scientific-computing
